sth:automatic_test a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Automatic Test"@en ;
    sth:active_description "When the Active indicator is on, the current signal is stable."@en ;
    sth:current_plan_description "Current Plan displays the absolute path of the plan file currently being executed."@en ;
    sth:description "Automatic Test. In Automatic Test mode, check whether the Power, RSSI, and Active indicators are normal to confirm that the Smart Tool Holder is operating normally. Figure 50, Automatic Test page. Operation procedure: 1. Parameters (Figure 51). Current Plan displays the absolute path of the current plan file. LOAD CURRENT stores the currently configured MAC, Port, and Tool ID for subsequent operations. Target MAC sets the MAC address of the Smart Tool Holder to use. Target Port sets its port number. Target Tool ID sets the tool ID bound to the Smart Tool Holder. APPLY UPDATES saves the confirmed STH status updates to a JSON file for the next operation. Content displays Connection Check and Save Settings updates after APPLY UPDATES so all parameters can be verified. 2. Action (Figure 52). LOAD ALL loads the STH connection and data-processing programs (STHComm, DataProcess) in preparation for Automatic Test. The data-processing program parses raw sensor TXT files into CSV files for analysis. ENABLE FUNC. starts the STH connection and data-processing programs. START RECORD records and processes STH sensor data into TXT files, which are subsequently processed and saved by DataProcess. Stop In Time(s) sets the automatic recording stop time in seconds. STOP RECORD stops recording and pauses sensor-data processing. DISABLE FUNC. pauses data processing and stops STH connection and data collection. UNLOAD ALL terminates all STH connection and data-processing programs and returns the system to the unmonitored state. 3. Online STH (Figure 53). Power displays the battery level of the enabled STH. RSSI displays current wireless signal strength for judging connection stability. Active on means stable signal and good connection. Hold on means unstable signal or interrupted STH connection and possibly incomplete data. STH ID displays the MAC address of the connected STH. Package ID increments for each packet received every 0.4 seconds and displays current connection data traffic. Recording Time displays elapsed recording time after START RECORD. Torque(Nm) and Bending X(N) display STH torque and bending-force data as line charts. 4. Logs (Figure 54). STH Comm log displays the STHComm.exe runtime log after LOAD ALL to show connection details. Data Process log displays the DataProcess.exe runtime log after LOAD ALL to track data-processing progress and status."@en ;
    sth:hold_description "When the Hold indicator is on, the current signal is unstable or the connection to the STH has been interrupted, resulting in incomplete received data."@en ;
    sth:package_id_description "Package ID increments each time a packet is received, every 0.4 seconds, and is used to display the current connection data traffic."@en ;
    sth:power_description "Power displays the remaining battery level of the currently enabled STH."@en ;
    sth:recording_time_description "Recording Time displays the elapsed recording time after START RECORD is pressed."@en ;
    sth:rssi_description "RSSI displays the current wireless signal strength of the connection."@en ;
    sth:sth_id_description "STH ID displays the MAC address of the currently connected STH."@en .

sth:available_sth_coefficient_file a sth:setting_item ;
    rdfs:label "AvailableSTH.csv"@en ;
    sth:description "Available STH coefficient file."@en .

