sth:case_1 a sth:abnormal_case ;
    rdfs:label "Power abnormality case 1"@en ;
    sth:applicable_question "This is a power-abnormality troubleshooting case, not the definition of Sleep-Wake Mode."@en ;
    sth:cause "The tool holder is in Sleep-Wake Mode."@en ;
    sth:complete_troubleshooting_steps "Connect the tool holder to the charging dock and complete charging, remove it, then shake it to enter Idle Mode. If no LED is still displayed at all, check the charging-dock contacts and adapter specifications or send the unit for repair."@en ;
    sth:description "If no LED is displayed after shaking the tool holder, the tool holder may be in Sleep-Wake Mode or have insufficient power. Connect it to the charging dock and complete charging, then remove it and shake it again to return it to an operational state."@en ;
    sth:non_status_mapping_table "This node is a power-abnormality troubleshooting case and answers only the causes and troubleshooting methods when no LED is displayed."@en ;
    sth:troubleshooting_method "Connect the tool holder to the charging dock and complete charging, remove it, then shake it to enter Idle Mode for normal use."@en .

sth:case_2 a sth:abnormal_case ;
    rdfs:label "After the tool holder is connected to the charging dock, the charging dock shows no LED."@en ;
    sth:cause "The charging contacts or adapter may be the problem."@en ;
    sth:complete_troubleshooting_steps "A. Check whether the charging contacts on the charging dock are correctly aligned with the charging contacts on the Smart Tool Holder. B. Check whether the charging dock adapter meets the requirements; the adapter output voltage should be DC 12V and the output current should be 2A. C. After replacing it with the required adapter, if charging still fails, the charging dock itself may be faulty. Contact the purchasing unit for repair service."@en ;
    sth:description "After the tool holder is connected to the charging dock, the charging dock shows no LED. Normally, the charging dock displays a red LED to indicate charging. If no LED is displayed, the charging contacts may not be aligned, the adapter may not meet specifications, or the charging dock may be faulty. A. Check whether the charging contacts on the charging dock correctly align with those on the Smart Tool Holder. B. Check whether the charging-dock adapter meets requirements; output voltage should be DC 12V and output current should be 2A. C. After replacing it with the required adapter, if charging still fails, the charging dock itself may be faulty; contact the purchasing unit for repair service."@en ;
    sth:non_status_mapping_table "This node is a no-LED troubleshooting case for the charging dock and answers only the causes and troubleshooting methods when the charging dock displays no LED."@en ;
    sth:possible_cause "Charging contacts not aligned, adapter does not meet specifications, or charging dock failure."@en ;
    sth:troubleshooting_method "Check whether the charging contacts are aligned; check whether the adapter output is DC 12V and 2A; if charging still fails, contact the purchasing unit for repair."@en .

sth:case_4 a sth:abnormal_case ;
    rdfs:label "Unable to connect to the tool holder"@en ;
    sth:cause "Available STHs already shows available tool holders, but LOAD ALL cannot connect."@en ;
    sth:description "Available STHs shows available tool holders, but LOAD ALL cannot connect. Available STHs displays the available Smart Tool Holders normally, but LOAD ALL cannot connect to them. Under normal conditions, the Logs continuously display information such as Target MAC and Port. When an error occurs, the condition is as shown in the figure. A. Check the MAC addresses and tool numbers of the Smart Tool Holders and tools that must be bound in the plan, such as the MAC addresses and tool numbers for STH1 and STH2 shown in the figure. B. Confirm that Smart Tool Holder-to-tool binding has been completed; use this button to bind the Smart Tool Holder MAC address to the tool number. C. Confirm that the APPLY UPDATES button in Save Settings has been clicked. D. After applying updates, confirm that the enabled Smart Tool Holder (Active STH) has a MAC address, as shown in the figure."@en ;
    sth:troubleshooting_method "Check the binding between the Smart Tool Holder MAC and tool number; confirm that BIND has been completed; confirm that APPLY UPDATES under Save Settings has been pressed and that Active STH has a MAC address."@en .

sth:case_5 a sth:abnormal_case ;
    rdfs:label "Excessive tool wear or damage"@en ;
    sth:cause "Torque data is abnormal in Simulation Analysis and exceeds UCL/LCL."@en ;
    sth:complete_troubleshooting_steps "A. Go to the Real-Time Monitoring page. B. Execute TOOL CHANGE to perform the tool-change operation."@en ;
    sth:description "When a tool is excessively worn or damaged, Simulation Analysis shows abnormal Torque (Nm) data exceeding the upper and lower control limits (UCL/LCL). Replace the tool before machining. A. Go to the Real-Time Monitoring page. B. Execute TOOL CHANGE to perform the tool-change operation."@en ;
    sth:tool_change_method "Go to the Real-Time Monitoring page and execute TOOL CHANGE to perform the tool-change operation."@en ;
    sth:troubleshooting_method "Go to the Real-Time Monitoring page and execute TOOL CHANGE to perform the tool change."@en .

sth:case_6 a sth:abnormal_case ;
    rdfs:label "Node-Red service paused; website not responding"@en ;
    sth:cause "A Node-Red service fault or a problematic .json file prevents the service from starting."@en ;
    sth:complete_troubleshooting_steps "If the Node-Red website does not respond, check the Node-Red status under Services in Task Manager. If it is paused and starting it has no effect, start Node-Red from Command Prompt (CMD). If 'Failed to stary server' appears, use the problematic .json file location indicated by the red box, delete or move that file, then start the Node-Red service again from CMD and reboot the computer."@en ;
    sth:description "Node-Red service paused; website not responding. If the Node-Red website does not respond, open Services in Task Manager and check the Node-Red status. If it is paused and starting it has no effect, start Node-Red from Command Prompt (CMD). If there is a problem, a screen like the figure will appear. If 'Failed to stary server' is shown, the red box below indicates the problematic .json file. Copy the file path on that line, delete the file or move it elsewhere, then restart the Node-Red service from Command Prompt (CMD) and reboot the computer to restore normal operation."@en ;
    sth:error_message "Failed to stary server" ;
    sth:troubleshooting_method "Start Node-Red from Command Prompt, remove or move the problematic .json file according to the error message, then restart the computer."@en .

