sth:data_settings_quick a sth:process_step ;
    rdfs:label "Data Settings"@en ;
    sth:description "Data Settings. Go to the Save Settings page (Figure 9). In Data Parsing (TXT->CSV), confirm whether raw data and parsed data such as CSV files need to be saved. These settings ensure subsequent data is stored correctly for further analysis. Ensure all settings have been applied using APPLY UPDATES so data can be saved properly during the experiment. Figure 9, Data Settings page."@en ;
    sth:txt_to_csv_settings "Go to the Save Settings page. In Data Parsing (TXT->CSV), confirm whether raw data and parsed data such as CSV files need to be saved, and confirm that all settings have been APPLY UPDATES."@en .

sth:data_view_quick a sth:process_step ;
    rdfs:label "Data Review"@en ;
    sth:add_control_limits_method "On the History Review page, first select Folder and File, then click ADD UCL LCL. The system adds upper and lower control limits to the selected CSV file, and the output filename is the original filename + _processed."@en,
        "On the History Review page, select Folder and File and then click ADD UCL LCL to add upper and lower control limits to the selected CSV file. The filename is the original filename + _processed."@en ;
    sth:control_limit_output_filename_rule "original filename + _processed"@en ;
    sth:description "Data Review. Select an effective time period for analysis: collected data must be analyzed effectively to obtain reliable conclusions. On the History Review page (Figure 11), select the data file to review and set a reasonable Time Interval to control display resolution. To observe upper and lower control limits, select Folder and File and click ADD UCL LCL; the selected CSV file will receive UCL/LCL and be named with the original filename + _processed. In the Summary area, view Start Time and End Time and select data from the stable machining stage. Confirm that channel maxima such as CH1 Max and CH2 Max are within reasonable ranges and that the Quality indicator passes (value 1). Simulation-result analysis: on the Simulation Analysis page, select the simulation CSV file to analyze and use line charts to inspect moment and position changes along different axes. The charts help explain the forces and displacement of the tool during machining. Figure 11, Data Review and Analysis page."@en ;
    sth:stable_machining_analysis_method "In the Summary area, view Start Time and End Time, select data from the stable machining stage for analysis, confirm that channel maxima such as CH1 Max and CH2 Max are within reasonable ranges, and verify that the Quality indicator is 1."@en .

sth:detection_item a sth:specification_item ;
    rdfs:label "Detection item"@en ;
    sth:value "Fx, Fy, Mz" .

sth:emc_test a sth:test_category ;
    rdfs:label "EMC"@en ;
