sth:integration_and_application a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Integration and Application"@en ;
    sth:description "Integration and Application"@en ;
    sth:has_subsection sth:integration_interface_example,
        sth:machining_history_example,
        sth:message_handshake_method ;
    sth:message_handshake_method "RPi/OT publishes information to the MQTT Broker, divided into four Topic categories. Edge/IT subscribes to Topics in the Broker to receive information. In the reverse direction, Edge/IT publishes to Topic: CMD/REQ, and RPi/OT then subscribes to the message."@en ;
    sth:monitor_detection_process_description "In the Monitor detection process, Edge can start, collect from, and stop the STH and can receive notifications such as tool breakage."@en ;
    sth:reference_detection_process_description "In the Reference process, Edge can start, receive, and stop; Pattern is used to start or stop comparison of whether the signal is normal."@en ;
    sth:standard_startup_process_description "During standard startup, Edge can obtain basic information such as the STH Mac connected to it and can perform time synchronization."@en ;
    sth:topic_category "CMD/REQ, CMD/RESP, CMD/NOTIFY, STH/Pdata, STH/FILE."@en .

sth:integration_interface_example a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Integration interface example"@en ;
    sth:cnc_tool_path_description "Displays CNC coordinate positions, allowing machining-path changes to be observed."@en ;
    sth:data_synchronization_process "First, use DTW (Dynamic Time Warping) on the CSV data from STH, SIM (simulation), and CTL (controller) to synchronize torque between the STH Torque field and SIM IsTouched field, and save the result as Torque_Sync.csv. Next, add the CTL Times and Offset Coordinates fields for time synchronization and save the result as Time_Sync.csv. Finally, send the synchronized result to the front end through WebSocket for display."@en ;
    sth:description "Integration Interface Example. First, CSV data from STH, SIM (simulation), and CTL (controller) are synchronized. Using DTW (Dynamic Time Warping), the STH Torque field and SIM IsTouched field are synchronized for torque, and the result is stored in Torque_Sync.csv, as shown in Figure 74. Next, the CTL Times and Offset Coordinates fields are added for time synchronization, and the result is stored in Time_Sync.csv, as shown in Figure 75. Finally, the synchronized result is sent to the front end through WebSocket for display, as shown in Figure 77. Figures 74 and 75 show the Torque_Sync.csv and Time_Sync.csv fields. CTL description: the Fanuc Focas2 API connects to the Fanuc controller to read information such as the CNC file name, G54 coordinates, and absolute coordinates, then stores the results as CSV. Referenced APIs are listed in Table 10. Figure 76, CTL file fields. Table 10, Focas2 functions: 1. NC program name — FWLIBAPI short WINAPI cnc_rdprgnum(unsigned short FlibHndl, ODBPRO *prgnum); 2. Absolute coordinate position of a specified axis — FWLIBAPI short WINAPI cnc_absolute(unsigned short FlibHndl, short axis, short length, ODBAXIS *absolute); 3. Workpiece zero-offset value (G54) for a specified number and axis — FWLIBAPI short WINAPI cnc_rdzofs(unsigned short FlibHndl, short number, short axis, short length, IODBZOFS *zofs); Figure 77, integrated STH and CNC display. Machining Parameters: reads parameters from config.json and displays Machine, Spindle Speed, Feed Rate, Program File, Tool Holder, STH Interval, Tool, ap (depth of cut), and ae (width of cut). Torque Over Time: x-axis is machining Time(s), y-axis is Torque(Nm); gray dashed Simulation Torque is simulated torque, red solid Real Torque is actual torque provided by STH, and green/orange dashed UCL/LCL are the upper/lower control limits based on simulated torque. Flute Profile: x-axis is CH1 and y-axis is CH2; 100 data points are displayed each time to represent the current flute profile. CNC Tool Path (mm): displays CNC coordinate positions to observe machining-path changes. STL Model: displays the simulated post-machining workpiece STL file."@en ;
    sth:flute_profile_description "The x-axis is CH1 and the y-axis is CH2. Using 100 data points per display can represent the flute profile of the current machining operation."@en ;
    sth:frontend_transmission_method "WebSocket" ;
    sth:machining_parameters_item "Machine, Spindle Speed, Feed Rate, Program File, Tool Holder, STH Interval, Tool, ap, ae."@en ;
    sth:machining_parameters_source "Read parameters from config.json."@en ;
    sth:stl_model_description "Displays the simulated post-machining workpiece STL file."@en ;
    sth:time_synchronization_method "Add the CTL Times and Offset Coordinates fields for time synchronization."@en ;
    sth:time_synchronization_output_file "Time_Sync.csv" ;
    sth:torque_over_time_description "The x-axis is machining Time(s) and the y-axis is Torque(Nm). The gray dashed Simulation Torque is simulated torque; the red solid Real Torque is actual STH torque; the green and orange dashed UCL and LCL respectively represent the upper and lower control limits based on simulated torque."@en ;
    sth:torque_synchronization_method "Use the DTW method to synchronize torque between the STH Torque field and the SIM IsTouched field."@en ;
    sth:torque_synchronization_output_file "Torque_Sync.csv" .

