sth:machining_history_example a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Machining history example"@en ;
    sth:basic_information "Includes machine ID (MC-001), tool holder name (TMV-720), controller (Fanuc), location (TT-F1-FAE), and tool holder type (BT-40)."@en ;
    sth:description "Machining history example. Introduction: This machining history is a record based on the STH body and Virtual Tool Room (VTR) system. It provides detailed data and analysis collected and recorded through the Smart Tool Holder and Virtual Tool Room during each CNC machining process. Main contents include: Basic information: machine ID (MC-001), tool holder name (TMV-720), controller (Fanuc), location (TT-F1-FAE), and tool holder type (BT-40), providing a complete description of the machining environment. Machining details: records the NC file (02420.nc), original STL file (Federal straight seam), design STL file (design.stl), machining material (FDAC/JIS SKD61), and workpiece number (K0001-1). Real-time data: presents torque variation over time as a chart for dynamic monitoring of the machining process. This machining history helps users quickly understand machining status and serves as a basis for subsequent optimization and abnormality diagnosis. Figure 78, machining-history PDF example."@en ;
    sth:file_purpose "A machining-history record is a document based on the Smart Tool Holder (STH) and Virtual Tool Room (VTR) systems. It provides detailed data and analysis collected and recorded through the Smart Tool Holder and Virtual Tool Room during each CNC machining process."@en ;
    sth:machining_details "Records the NC file (02420.nc), original STL file (Federal straight seam), design STL file (design.stl), machining material (FDAC/JIS SKD61), and workpiece number (K0001-1)."@en ;
    sth:real_time_data "Presents the change in torque over time as a chart, providing a dynamic monitoring reference for the machining process."@en .

