sth:message_handshake_method a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Message handshake method"@en ;
    sth:description "Message Handshake Method. RPi/OT publishes information to the MQTT Broker in four Topic categories, and Edge/IT subscribes to Broker Topics to receive information. In the reverse direction, Edge/IT publishes to Topic: CMD/REQ and RPi/OT subscribes to the message, as shown in Figure 65. Topic field definitions are shown in Figure 66, CMD_REQ JSON fields; Figure 67, CMD/RESP JSON fields; Figure 68, CMD/NOTIFY JSON fields; Figure 69, STH/Pdata JSON fields; and Figure 70, STH/FILE JSON fields. Topic CMD/REQ: Edge sends a command; after Edge/IT sends CMD/REQ, Pi responds according to the command with CMD/RESP. Topic 1: CMD/RESP, command execution result. Topic 2: CMD/NOTIFY, proactive notification. Topic 3: STH/Pdata, proactive real-time sensor-data report. Topic 4: STH/FILE, file transfer. Based on these message formats, different processes can be constructed, including Standard Startup, Monitor Detection, and Reference Detection. During standard startup, Edge obtains basic information such as the connected STH Mac and can perform time synchronization (Figure 71). In Monitor Detection, Edge can start, collect from, and stop the STH and can receive notifications such as tool breakage (Figure 72). In Reference Detection, Edge can start, receive, and stop, while Pattern is used to start or stop comparison of whether the signal is normal (Figure 73)."@en ;
    sth:has_topic sth:CMD_NOTIFY,
        sth:CMD_REQ,
        sth:CMD_RESP,
        sth:STH_FILE,
        sth:STH_Pdata .

sth:minimum_recording_threshold a sth:setting_item ;
    rdfs:label "Threshold for Keep Data(Nm)"@en ;
