    sth:default_location "C:\\VTR\\RawData\\Output\\*.csv" ;
    sth:description "Set the default STH output file path used to store parsed data."@en,
        "Stores parsed CSV data."@en ;
    sth:value "C:\\VTR\\RawData\\Output\\*.csv" .

sth:production_plan_settings_detailed a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "VTR Plan page operation procedure"@en ;
    sth:description "Plan Settings. Figure 27, Plan Settings page. Operation procedure: 1. Create and update plans (Figure 28). NEW PLAN: press NEW PLAN to start a new production or experimental plan. A new plan file is created in which all required machine, tool, and workpiece parameters can be configured. New plans are saved in JSON and YML formats and include basic settings such as date, machine location, and plan type. UPDATE PLAN: use UPDATE PLAN to modify an existing plan, such as changing machine configuration or tool parameters. The updated plan overwrites the existing version and all changes are displayed in Plan Updates for tracking. Reload Plan: use Reload Plan to reload a previous plan and view its settings. 2. Configure machine, tool, and machining mode (Figure 29). In Machine-Part-Tool Holder, configure basic machine information such as Machine ID, Type, Controller, and Machining mode to record different machines and machining modes. Design STL and Material: upload the workpiece STL and select the workpiece material. To bind Smart Tool Holders and tools required by the plan, select a MAC under STH and a tool number under TID. BIND binds the MAC of a Smart Tool Holder such as STH1 or STH2 to a tool number such as TID1 or TID2 to ensure correct recording and tool use. CLEAR BIND removes the current binding between tool and tool holder. 3. Configure tool parameters (Figure 30). In each T1–T5 area, set Tool ID, Diameter, Flute Num, Full Height, and Flute Height. Also record tool wear before and after machining for tool-life analysis and production optimization. These settings are saved in the plan file and displayed in Plan Updates. 4. View plan update records (Figure 31). Plan Updates displays all updates made to the production plan. Whenever UPDATE PLAN is pressed or another plan change is made, the change is recorded here in JSON format."@en ;
    sth:how_to_bind_smart_tool_holder_and_tool "On the Plan Settings page, select the Smart Tool Holder MAC under STH and the tool number under TID, then click BIND to bind the Smart Tool Holder and the tool."@en ;
    sth:node_boundary "This node answers only the VTR Plan / Plan Settings page operation procedure; it does not answer the configurable parameters of Smart Tool Holder Configuration Mode."@en ;
    sth:not_applicable_question "What can be configured in Smart Tool Holder Configuration Mode?"@en,
        "What parameters can Configuration Mode configure?"@en,
        "Which parameters can be configured while the Smart Tool Holder is in Configuration Mode?"@en ;
    sth:smart_tool_holder_tool_binding_answer "On the Plan Settings page, select the Smart Tool Holder MAC under STH and the tool number under TID, then click BIND to complete the binding."@en .

sth:production_plan_settings_quick a sth:process_step ;
    rdfs:label "VTR Plan page quick procedure"@en ;
    sth:description "Plan Settings. Go to the Plan Settings page (Figure 7), press NEW PLAN to create a new production or experimental plan, configure Machine ID, material, machining mode, tool holder MAC and Port, and bind the corresponding Tool ID. To update an existing plan, use UPDATE PLAN. Use BIND to bind each Smart Tool Holder MAC to the corresponding tool number. Figure 7, Plan Settings page."@en ;
    sth:how_to_bind_smart_tool_holder_and_tool "On the Plan Settings page, select the Smart Tool Holder MAC under STH and the tool number under TID, then click BIND to bind the Smart Tool Holder and the tool."@en ;
    sth:node_boundary "This node answers only the VTR Plan / Plan Settings page operation procedure; it does not answer the configurable parameters of Smart Tool Holder Configuration Mode."@en ;
    sth:not_applicable_question "What can be configured in Smart Tool Holder Configuration Mode?"@en,
        "What parameters can Configuration Mode configure?"@en,
        "Which parameters can be configured while the Smart Tool Holder is in Configuration Mode?"@en ;
    sth:smart_tool_holder_tool_binding_answer "On the Plan Settings page, select the Smart Tool Holder MAC under STH and the tool number under TID, then click BIND to complete the binding."@en .

sth:raw_data_directory_location a sth:setting_item ;
    rdfs:label "Raw Data Folder Location"@en ;
    sth:default_location "C:\\VTR\\RawData\\Source\\Data\\*.txt" ;
    sth:description "Set the directory location for Smart Tool Holder raw data."@en,
        "Stores detected raw TXT data."@en ;
    sth:value "C:\\VTR\\RawData\\Source\\Data\\*.txt" .

sth:real_time_monitoring a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Real-Time Monitoring"@en ;
    sth:description "Real-Time Monitoring. Figure 45, Real-Time Monitoring page. Operation procedure: 1. Action area (Figure 46). LOAD ALL: loads the STH connection and data-processing programs (STHComm, DataProcess) to begin real-time monitoring. The data-processing program parses raw sensor TXT files into CSV files for data analysis. ENABLE FUNC.: starts the STH connection and data-processing programs so the system can receive STH data. START RECORD: starts recording and processing STH sensor data into TXT files; the data is subsequently processed and saved by DataProcess. SEND JOB: sends the selected job from the Job list to runSTHJobs.py through MQTT for specific STH operations. Stop In Time(s): automatically stops recording after the specified number of seconds. TOOL CHANGE: triggers a CNC tool-change action. STOP RECORD: stops recording and pauses sensor-data processing. DISABLE FUNC.: pauses data processing and stops the STH connection and data collection. UNLOAD ALL: terminates all STH connection and data-processing programs and returns the system to the unmonitored state. 2. Online STH (Figure 47). Current Plan: displays the absolute path of the currently executing plan file. Package ID: increments for every packet received at 0.4-second intervals and indicates current connection data traffic. STH ID: displays the MAC address of the connected STH. RSSI: displays the current wireless signal strength. Power: displays the remaining battery level of the enabled STH. Recording Time: displays elapsed recording time after START RECORD is pressed. Active: when lit, the signal is stable. Hold: when lit, the signal is unstable or the STH connection is interrupted, causing incomplete data. 3. STH Data (Figure 48). Torque (Nm): line chart of torque read by the STH. Bending X (N): line chart of bending force read by the STH. 4. Logs (Figure 49). STH Comm log: after LOAD ALL, displays the STHComm.exe runtime log for connection details. Data Process log: after LOAD ALL, displays the DataProcess.exe runtime log for tracking data-processing progress and status."@en ;
    sth:monitoring_field "Current Plan, Package ID, STH ID, RSSI, Power, Recording Time, Active, Hold, Torque(Nm), Bending X(N)" ;
    sth:sensor_data_recording_method "Press START RECORD to begin recording and processing STH sensor data into TXT files. The data is subsequently processed and saved through DataProcess."@en ;
    sth:tool_change_function "When a CNC tool change is required, press this button to trigger the tool-change action."@en ;
    sth:tool_change_method "When a CNC tool change is required, press TOOL CHANGE on the Real-Time Monitoring page to trigger the tool-change action."@en ;
    sth:tool_change_operation "When a CNC tool change is required, press TOOL CHANGE on the Real-Time Monitoring page to trigger the tool-change action."@en ;
    sth:tool_change_tool_change_function "When a CNC tool change is required, press TOOL CHANGE to trigger the tool-change action."@en ;
    sth:viewable_item sth:sufficient_signal_strength_judgment .

sth:root_directory_location a sth:setting_item ;
    rdfs:label "Root Folder Location"@en ;
    sth:default_location "C:\\VTR" ;
    sth:description "Set the root directory location for Virtual Tool Room data."@en,
        "Virtual Tool Room root directory"@en ;
    sth:value "C:\\VTR" .

sth:rssi_insufficient_rescan_condition_direct_qa a sth:qa_anchor ;
    rdfs:label "RSSI rescan condition"@en ;
    sth:answer "RSSI ≤ -50 dB between the Smart Tool Holder and Router indicates insufficient signal strength, which may cause connection interruption or incomplete data; therefore, the Smart Tool Holder must be rescanned."@en ;
    sth:cause_description "RSSI ≤ -50 dB means the signal strength between the Smart Tool Holder and Router is insufficient, which may cause connection interruption or incomplete data."@en ;
    sth:corresponding_topic sth:connection_check,
        sth:sufficient_signal_strength_judgment ;
    sth:question "Under what circumstances does the Smart Tool Holder need to be rescanned?"@en,
        "Under what conditions does the Smart Tool Holder need to be rescanned?"@en,
        "When does the Smart Tool Holder need to be rescanned?"@en ;
    sth:rescan_condition "RSSI ≤ -50 dB between the Smart Tool Holder and Router indicates insufficient signal strength, which may cause connection interruption or incomplete data; therefore, the Smart Tool Holder must be rescanned."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "RSSI rescan condition"@en .

sth:setting_js a sth:file ;
    rdfs:label "setting.js"@en ;
    sth:description "Node-Red configuration file. setting.js contains flowFile: 'VTR_flows(YYYYMMDDV).json' and functionGlobalContext, including modules such as fs, csv-parser, path, async, js-yaml, and os."@en ;
    sth:setting_content "flowFile: 'VTR_flows(YYYYMMDDV).json'; functionGlobalContext: { fs, csv, path, async, yaml, os }" .

sth:setting_mode_read a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Configuration Mode - Read"@en ;
    sth:description "Configuration Mode - Read. Table 8, Configuration Mode - Read. Function / Edge Command / WSB Response. 1. Read Router SSID: rssid\\n / rssid:setting value\\n / read Router SSID. 2. Read Password: rpass\\n / rpass:setting value\\n / read Router Password setting value. 3. Read IP: rip\\n / rip:setting value\\n / read IP setting value. 4. Read port: rport\\n / rport:setting value\\n / read port setting value. 5. Read RF Power Level: rpower\\n / rpower:setting value\\n / 1–5, default 5; (5, 8.5, 13, 16.5, 19.5) dBm. 6. Read G-threshold: rgsensor\\n / rgsensor:setting value\\n / read G-Sensor sensitivity. 7. Read sleep time: rctime\\n / rctime:setting value\\n / read sleep time. 8. Read polling interval: rptime\\n / rptime:setting value\\n / read polling interval. 9. Read voltage: rbat\\n / rbat:actual voltage\\n / read current battery voltage. 10. Read signal strength: rRSSI\\n / rRSSI:received signal strength\\n / read current received signal strength. 11. Read program version: rVER\\n / rVER:<M>core 1 version,<E>core 2 version\\n / read the program versions of the two WSB cores, e.g. rVER:<M>01.11,<E>02.03. 12. Continue synchronization: syn\\n / syn:OK\\n / Configuration Mode has a 2-minute timeout. If Edge cannot send configuration data within 2 minutes, it must send syn to the Wireless Sensing Board (WSB), otherwise the channel is considered disconnected."@en ;
    sth:has_command sth:continue_synchronization_command,
        sth:read_g_threshold_command,
        sth:read_ip_command,
        sth:read_password_command,
        sth:read_polling_interval_command,
        sth:read_port_command,
        sth:read_program_version_command,
        sth:read_rf_power_command,
        sth:read_router_ssid_command,
        sth:read_signal_strength_command,
        sth:read_sleep_time_command,
        sth:read_voltage_command .

sth:setting_mode_write a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Configuration Mode - Write"@en ;
    sth:configurable_parameter "Router SSID, Password, IP, Port, RF Power Level, G-threshold, polling interval, sleep time."@en ;
    sth:description "Configuration Mode - Write. Table 7, Configuration Mode - Write. Function / Edge Command / WSB Response. 1. Return to Transmission Mode: exit\\n / Exit Configuration Mode\\n / leave Configuration Mode and return to Transmission Mode. 2. Set Router SSID: ssid: ST_route \\n / SSID setting “ST_route” OK\\n / set Router SSID to ST_route. 3. Set Password: pass:123456abc\\n / Password setting “123456abc” OK\\n / set Router Password to 123456abc. 4. Set IP: ip:1.1.1.102\\n / IP setting “1.1.1.102” OK\\n / set IP to 1.1.1.102. 5. Set port: port:6500\\n / Port setting “6500” OK\\n / set port to 6500. 6. Set RF Power Level: power:3\\n / RF TX Power setting “3” OK\\n / 1–5, default 2; (5, 8.5, 13, 16.5, 19.5) dBm. 7. Set wake-up G-threshold: gsensor:10\\n / G-Sensor setting “10” OK\\n / set G-Sensor sensitivity to 10 (range 1–64, default 4). Setting 1–63: vibration-mode sensitivity. Setting 64: angle wake-up (80°). 8. Set sleep time: ctime:60\\n / ctime setting “60” OK\\n / set sleep time to 60 s (range 20–255 s, default 30 s). 9. Set polling interval: ptime:8\\n / ptime setting “8” OK\\n / set ptime to 8 during sleep (setting range 0–5760, default 0). Setting 0: no periodic polling during sleep. Setting 1–5760: sleep interval, base unit 15 s. 10. Enter Sleep Mode: sleep\\n / Enter Sleep Mode\\n / leave Configuration Mode and enter Sleep Mode."@en ;
    sth:has_command sth:enter_sleep_mode_command,
        sth:return_to_transmission_mode,
        sth:set_g_threshold_command,
        sth:set_ip_command,
        sth:set_password_command,
        sth:set_polling_interval_command,
        sth:set_port_command,
        sth:set_rf_power_command,
        sth:set_router_ssid_command,
        sth:set_sleep_time_command ;
    sth:setting_mode_configurable_parameters_query sth:smart_tool_holder_setting_mode_configurable_parameters .

sth:simulation_analysis a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Simulation Analysis"@en ;
    sth:description "Simulation Analysis. Figure 61, Simulation Analysis page. Operation procedure: 1. Action area (Figure 62). Current Plan displays the current plan file so the user knows which plan is being analyzed. UPDATE NC FILE updates the target NC filename according to the Settings page to manage and synchronize the latest NC program. NC File displays the current target NC filename. Select File selects a CSV file that already contains simulation results for analysis. Time Interval displays the interval n between displayed data points (0.003*n sec) to control data-review resolution. 2. Simulation Data (Figure 63). Moment Z and Moment Y display the average Z-axis and Y-axis moment data in the selected simulation CSV file as line charts. UCL is the Upper Control Limit; LCL is the Lower Control Limit. The charts visually show average Z- and Y-axis moment changes over time and help explain forces on the tool during simulation. Coordinate X, Coordinate Y, and Coordinate Z display X-, Y-, and Z-axis position changes in the simulation data as line charts. To view the simulated tool movement trajectory, examine the Coordinate X, Coordinate Y, and Coordinate Z charts to understand position changes in different directions during simulation."@en ;
    sth:simulated_tool_movement_trajectory_chart "Coordinate X, Coordinate Y, Coordinate Z"@en ;
    sth:simulated_tool_movement_trajectory_viewing_method "View the Coordinate X, Coordinate Y, and Coordinate Z charts to understand the tool's position changes in different directions during simulation."@en .

sth:standby_time a sth:direct_answer_node,
        sth:qa_anchor,
        sth:specification_item ;
    rdfs:label "Standby time"@en ;
    sth:answer ">10 day"@en ;
    sth:belongs_to_specification sth:general_specification ;
    sth:complete_answer "The Smart Tool Holder power-supply standby time is >10 day."@en ;
    sth:direct_answer ">10 day"@en ;
    sth:node_boundary "This node answers only the power-supply standby time in the Smart Tool Holder general specifications; the direct answer is >10 day. It does not answer configurable parameters in Configuration Mode or sleep-time setting items."@en ;
    sth:not_used_as_answer "Smart Tool Holder power-supply standby time"@en ;
    sth:power_supply_standby_time ">10 day"@en ;
    sth:question "How long is the Smart Tool Holder standby time?"@en,
        "How many days is the Smart Tool Holder standby time?"@en,
        "What is the Smart Tool Holder power-supply standby time?"@en,
        "What is the standby time of the power supply?"@en ;
