sth:qa_sleep_wake_mode_answer a sth:mode ;
    rdfs:label "After a polling interval is configured, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state. In this mode, it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge. After receiving it, Edge can reply as needed with a command that returns WSB to Sleep Mode or places it in Idle Mode."@en,
        "qa_sleep_wake_mode_answer"@en ;
    sth:answer "After a polling interval is configured, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state; in this mode it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge. After receiving it, Edge can reply as needed with a command to return WSB to Sleep Mode or place it in Idle Mode."@en ;
    sth:available_reply_command "After receiving the Header, Edge can reply with two types of commands: 1. reply with the Enter Sleep Mode command to return WSB to Sleep Mode; 2. reply with the Enter Idle Mode command to place WSB in Idle Mode and resume normal startup."@en ;
    sth:definition "After a polling interval is configured, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state."@en ;
    sth:description "After a polling interval is configured, WSB periodically leaves Sleep Mode and enters a brief wake state. In this mode, it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge; after receiving it, Edge can reply to WSB with a command as needed."@en ;
    sth:enter_idle_mode_command_description "Reply with the Enter Idle Mode command to place WSB in Idle Mode and resume normal startup."@en ;
    sth:enter_sleep_mode_command_description "Reply with the Enter Sleep Mode command to return WSB to Sleep Mode."@en ;
    sth:question "What is Sleep-Wake Mode?"@en ;
    sth:reported_content "In Sleep-Wake Mode, one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) is reported to Edge."@en ;
    sth:sleep_wake_mode_definition "After a polling interval is configured, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state; in this mode it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge. After receiving it, Edge can reply as needed with a command to return WSB to Sleep Mode or place it in Idle Mode."@en ;
    sth:sleep_wake_mode_definition_answer "After a polling interval is configured, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state; in this mode it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge. After receiving it, Edge can reply as needed with a command to return WSB to Sleep Mode or place it in Idle Mode."@en ;
    sth:what_is_sleep_wake_mode "After a polling interval is configured, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state; in this mode it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge. After receiving it, Edge can reply as needed with a command to return WSB to Sleep Mode or place it in Idle Mode."@en .

sth:smart_tool_holder_advanced_settings a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Smart Tool Holder - Advanced Settings"@en ;
    sth:description "Smart Tool Holder - Advanced Settings. The Smart Tool Holder (STH) contains a Wireless Sensing Board (WSB). During use, the STH connects to Edge through a Router using TCP/IP. Edge can send commands through TCP/IP; the STH executes the commands and returns messages to Edge. The Smart Tool Holder has five main operating modes: Idle, Transmission, Configuration, Sleep, and Sleep-Wake, with transitions shown in Figure 64. After power is supplied and Reset is performed, the STH enters Idle Mode. Before connection, this mode checks internal components, voltage, and other internal STH abnormalities; LED indications are shown in Table 4. In Idle or Configuration Mode, when the preset time is exceeded or a sleep command is received, the STH enters Sleep Mode. In Configuration Mode, when an Edge connection or transmission command is received, the STH enters Transmission Mode; LED indications are shown in Table 4. In Sleep Mode, when motion exceeding the G-threshold is detected, the STH leaves Sleep Mode, first enters Idle Mode, and returns to Transmission Mode after connecting to Edge. G Sensor sensitivity uses the full setting range 1–63, default 4. In Configuration Mode, configurable parameters include Router SSID, Password, IP, Port, RF Power Level, G-threshold, polling interval, and sleep time. Sleep-Wake Mode: after configuring a polling interval, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state. In this mode it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge. Edge can reply with either: 1. Enter Sleep Mode command, returning WSB to Sleep Mode; or 2. Enter Idle Mode command, placing WSB in Idle Mode and resuming normal startup. Table 4, Smart Tool Holder mode LEDs: Mode / Status / LED (RGB) Green Blue Red. Initial: initialize device — -/-/-. Idle: initialization completed — green solid for 5 s; normal vibration-started but not connected — green 50 ms / 1 s; abnormality detected at power-on — red solid; low voltage — red 50 ms / 3 s. Sleep: device sleeping — no LED. Wake: RTC started but not connected — green 50 ms / 2.5 s. Transmission: TCP packet channel enabled — blue 50 ms / 1 s. Configuration: TCP packet channel enabled — blue solid."@en ;
    sth:has_mode sth:qa_sleep_wake_mode_answer ;
    sth:has_subsection sth:connection_settings,
        sth:mode_switching,
        sth:setting_mode_read,
        sth:setting_mode_write,
        sth:sleep_mode,
        sth:transmission_mode ;
    sth:setting_mode_configurable_parameters "Router SSID, Password, IP, Port, RF Power Level, G-threshold, polling interval, sleep time."@en ;
    sth:setting_mode_configurable_parameters_query sth:smart_tool_holder_setting_mode_configurable_parameters ;
    sth:sleep_wake_mode_definition "After a polling interval is configured, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state; in this mode it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge."@en ;
    sth:sleep_wake_mode_description "After a polling interval is configured, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state; in this mode it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge."@en .

