sth:mode_switching a sth:section ;
    rdfs:label "Smart Tool Holder mode LED status mapping"@en ;
    sth:angle_wake_up_condition "The G Sensor setting can be configured for angle wake-up (setting value 64). The device can be awakened whenever the tool holder angle changes by more than 80°."@en ;
    sth:blue_led_answer "A blue LED on the Smart Tool Holder means the TCP packet channel is enabled and the Smart Tool Holder is in Transmission Mode or normally connected."@en ;
    sth:blue_led_status "TCP packet channel enabled, indicating that the Smart Tool Holder is in Transmission Mode or normally connected."@en ;
    sth:description "Mode Switching. Startup mode: during power-on startup and operation, the tool holder dynamically checks internal Sensor ICs. If the MCU detects a connection problem with any internal Sensor IC, the Smart Tool Holder displays a red LED. Continuing to use the tool holder may cause abnormal operation. When an abnormal LED appears, first confirm that the tool holder power supply is normal and try power-cycling it. If the abnormal LED still appears after restart, return it to the manufacturer for inspection and repair. Sleep Mode: conditions for entering Sleep Mode after startup include a configurable sleep-entry time (20–255 seconds, default 30); TCP SOCKET channel disconnected for more than 30 seconds (default) during machining/tool-magazine status; G Sensor wake-up/transport status without Router connection for more than 60 seconds (default); or TCP SOCKET channel disconnected for more than 30 seconds (default) in Configuration Mode. Wake Mode: before transport, the G Sensor can be set to angle wake-up (setting value 64). In this mode the device is less likely to wake from vibration, but an angle change greater than 80° easily wakes it. Waking from Sleep Mode, connecting to the router, and entering Transmission Mode normally completes within 10 seconds. The Smart Tool Holder can be awakened by shaking it beyond the G-threshold. Configuration Mode: RF Power can be configured with Power Level 1–5, default 2: 1=5 dBm, 2=8.5 dBm, 3=13 dBm, 4=16.5 dBm, 5=19.5 dBm. The polling interval can be set from 15 s to 1 day, default disabled, allowing periodic wake-up from Sleep Mode; this state is Sleep-Wake Mode. In Sleep-Wake Mode, the device remains associated with configured Router 1 and periodically reports battery level and other information. If configured Router 1 is not found within the sleep-time limit, it returns to Sleep Mode."@en ;
    sth:has_mode sth:qa_sleep_wake_mode_answer ;
    sth:led_target "Smart Tool Holder"@en ;
    sth:method_to_wake_up_smart_tool_holder "Shake the Smart Tool Holder beyond the G-threshold to wake it."@en,
        "Shake the Smart Tool Holder beyond the G-threshold to wake it. After waking, it first enters Idle Mode and returns to Transmission Mode after the connection is completed."@en ;
    sth:mode_list "Idle Mode, Transmission Mode, Configuration Mode, Sleep Mode, Sleep-Wake Mode."@en ;
    sth:operating_mode "Idle, Transmission, Configuration, Sleep, and Sleep-Wake modes."@en ;
    sth:question "How can I wake up the Smart Tool Holder?"@en,
        "How do I wake the Smart Tool Holder while it is in Sleep Mode?"@en,
        "What condition does a red LED on the Smart Tool Holder indicate?"@en,
        "What does a blue indicator on the Smart Tool Holder mean?"@en,
        "What does it mean when the Smart Tool Holder displays a blue LED?"@en,
        "What does it mean when the Smart Tool Holder displays a red LED?"@en,
        "What does the Smart Tool Holder's red LED indicate?"@en,
        "What is the procedure for waking up the Smart Tool Holder?"@en ;
    sth:red_led_abnormal_situation "A red LED on the Smart Tool Holder means that the MCU has detected a connection problem with one of the internal Sensor ICs."@en ;
    sth:red_led_situation "A red LED on the Smart Tool Holder means that the MCU has detected a connection problem with one of the internal Sensor ICs."@en ;
    sth:red_led_situation_answer "The MCU has detected a connection problem with one of the internal Sensor ICs. Tool holder operation may be abnormal. First verify the power supply and try power-cycling the tool holder. If the red LED still appears after restart, return it to the manufacturer for inspection and repair."@en ;
    sth:situation "A red LED on the Smart Tool Holder means that the MCU has detected a connection problem with one of the internal Sensor ICs. Tool holder operation may be abnormal; check the power supply and try power-cycling. If the red LED still appears after restart, return the unit to the manufacturer for inspection and repair."@en ;
    sth:sleep_wake_condition "Shake the Smart Tool Holder beyond the G-threshold to wake it."@en ;
    sth:sleep_wake_mode_definition "After a polling interval is configured, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state; in this mode it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge. After receiving it, Edge can reply as needed with a command to return WSB to Sleep Mode or place it in Idle Mode."@en ;
    sth:sleep_wake_mode_description "After a polling interval is configured, WSB can periodically leave Sleep Mode and enter a brief wake state; in this mode it reports one Header (packet sequence number: 99999) to Edge."@en ;
    sth:sleep_wake_process "After motion exceeding the G-threshold is detected in Sleep Mode, the Smart Tool Holder leaves Sleep Mode, first enters Idle Mode, and switches back to Transmission Mode after the connection to Edge is completed."@en ;
    sth:sleep_wake_to_transmission_time "After waking from Sleep Mode, connecting to the router and entering Transmission Mode normally takes about 10 seconds."@en ;
    sth:smart_tool_holder_red_led_answer "A red LED on the Smart Tool Holder means that the MCU has detected a connection problem with one of the internal Sensor ICs. Tool holder operation may be abnormal; first confirm that the power supply is normal and try power-cycling the tool holder. If the abnormal LED still appears after restart, return it to the manufacturer for inspection and repair."@en ;
    sth:transmission_mode_blue_led_status "TCP packet channel enabled, indicating that the Smart Tool Holder is in Transmission Mode; in the LED table, the blue LED flashes at 50 ms / 1 s."@en ;
    sth:wake_up_method "Shake the Smart Tool Holder beyond the G-threshold to wake it."@en ;
    sth:what_are_smart_tool_holder_operating_modes "The Smart Tool Holder has five main operating modes: Idle, Transmission, Configuration, Sleep, and Sleep-Wake."@en ;
    sth:what_does_blue_led_on_smart_tool_holder_mean "A blue LED on the Smart Tool Holder means the TCP packet channel is enabled and the Smart Tool Holder is in Transmission Mode or normally connected."@en ;
    sth:what_does_red_led_on_smart_tool_holder_mean "A red LED on the Smart Tool Holder means that the MCU has detected a connection problem with one of the internal Sensor ICs."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Smart Tool Holder mode LED status mapping"@en .

sth:sufficient_signal_strength_judgment a sth:process_step ;
    rdfs:label "Sufficient signal-strength judgment"@en ;
    sth:check_item "RSSI" ;
    sth:check_location "Real-Time Monitoring page"@en ;
    sth:description "Signal strength can be viewed on the Real-Time Monitoring page. When RSSI > -50 dB, the signal strength between the Smart Tool Holder and Router is sufficient. When RSSI ≤ -50 dB, signal strength is insufficient and may cause connection interruption or incomplete data."@en ;
    sth:insufficient_condition "RSSI ≤ -50 dB" ;
    sth:insufficient_description "Indicates insufficient signal strength, which may cause connection interruption or incomplete data"@en ;
    sth:insufficient_effect "May cause connection interruption or incomplete data."@en ;
    sth:insufficient_handling_method "When RSSI ≤ -50 dB, insufficient signal strength may cause connection interruption or incomplete data, so the Smart Tool Holder must be rescanned."@en ;
    sth:judgment_method "When RSSI > -50 dB, the signal strength between the Smart Tool Holder and Router is sufficient; when RSSI ≤ -50 dB, signal strength is insufficient and may cause connection interruption or incomplete data."@en ;
    sth:rescan_condition_query sth:rssi_insufficient_rescan_condition_direct_qa ;
    sth:sufficient_condition "RSSI > -50 dB" ;
    sth:sufficient_description "Indicates that the signal strength between the Smart Tool Holder and Router is sufficient"@en ;
    sth:view_location "Signal strength can be viewed on the Real-Time Monitoring page."@en ;
    skos:altLabel "RSSI check"@en,
        "STH signal-strength judgment"@en,
        "Signal-strength check"@en,
        "Smart Tool Holder signal-strength judgment"@en .

